@page "/van-sales/routes"
@attribute [Authorize(Roles = "Admin,Manager")]
@rendermode InteractiveServer
@using ShopInventory.Web.Models
@inject IVanSalesReportService VanSalesReportService

<PageTitle>Selling Routes - Shop Inventory</PageTitle>

@* The route master. Selling Routes.dc.html.

   Carried by the `vsr-` block at the foot of wwwroot/css/van-sales.css (linked
   from App.razor) in both schemes.

   Small on purpose — four fields — but the compliance report cannot say a word
   about territory, route or truck registration without it, because none of the
   three existed as data anywhere before this. A van points at a route; the route
   says these things once, so a report can group by them without free text
   fragmenting "Guruve" into three routes.

   There is no delete. A route names trading days that have already happened, and
   those days keep a snapshot of its code and name so a rename cannot rewrite
   history — but removing the row would still orphan the live assignments. Retire
   it instead, which the server refuses while vans are still on it.

   Each row opens its own schedule in place — the areas it works, and when. A town
   truck keeps a weekday and no cycle week; an upcountry route keeps a cycle week
   and no weekday, because the trip is away for days at a time and the schedule
   commits to the week rather than to which morning the van reaches Chiredzi. Null
   in either column therefore means something, and the two controls read "No fixed
   day" and "Every week" rather than defaulting to Monday and week 1. A stop
   dropped here is deactivated rather than deleted, so the seeder does not put it
   back on the next start.

   Three things the redesign decided, each of which is a claim about the data
   rather than a matter of taste:

   - **The strip is a per-route census.** A town truck's cells are MON…FRI; an
     upcountry round's are W1, W2. The cells always sum to the Stops column beside
     them — see StripFor, which adds a trailing cell for anything the route's own
     shape does not cover rather than letting it fall off the end.

   - **The week is shown whole, but only where there is a week.** A route that
     keeps weekdays gets a lane for every one of Monday to Friday even when the
     lane is empty, because "nothing on Thursday" is the thing a planner is
     looking for. A route that keeps cycle weeks gets only the lanes it has;
     drawing it five empty weekdays would invent a shape it does not run to.

   - **The guidance line is conditional.** "No trucks or vans are linked yet"
     is true of a fresh install and false of this one, and a permanent banner
     saying it reads as a fault report rather than as a next step. *@

<div class="vs">

    <div class="vs-head">
        <div>
            <h2 class="vs-title">Selling routes</h2>
            <p class="vs-subtitle">
                Each route is the round one van runs: its territory, the truck normally assigned to it
                and the areas it works, day by day. A van joins a route from its own user account.
            </p>
        </div>
        <div class="vs-actions">
            <button class="vs-btn vs-btn-accent" @onclick="StartNew" disabled="@(isSaving || IsAddingNew)">
                <i class="ph ph-plus" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                Add route
            </button>
        </div>
    </div>

    @if (error is not null)
    {
        <div class="vs-notice">@error</div>
    }

    <div class="vsr-stats">
        <span class="vsr-stat">
            <span class="vsr-stat-n">@routes.Count(route => route.IsActive)</span>
            <span class="vsr-stat-l">active @(routes.Count(route => route.IsActive) == 1 ? "route" : "routes")</span>
        </span>
        <span class="vsr-stat">
            <span class="vsr-stat-n">@stops.Count</span>
            <span class="vsr-stat-l">stops planned</span>
        </span>
        <span class="vsr-stat">
            <span class="vsr-stat-n">@Territories.Count</span>
            <span class="vsr-stat-l">@(Territories.Count == 1 ? "territory" : "territories")</span>
        </span>
        @if (NothingIsLinked)
        {
            <p class="vsr-note">
                <i class="ph ph-truck" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                No trucks or vans are linked yet — assign them from each van's user account.
            </p>
        }
    </div>

    @if (IsAddingNew)
    {
        <section class="vsr-panel">
            <h3 class="vsr-panel-title">New route</h3>
            <p class="vsr-panel-sub">Give it a code and a name, then add its stops once it is saved.</p>
            <div class="vsr-form">
                <div class="vsr-field">
                    <label class="vs-filter-label" for="vsr-code">Code</label>
                    <input id="vsr-code" class="vs-field" @bind="editing!.Code" placeholder="GUR" />
                </div>
                <div class="vsr-field">
                    <label class="vs-filter-label" for="vsr-name">Name</label>
                    <input id="vsr-name" class="vs-field" @bind="editing!.Name" placeholder="Guruve" />
                </div>
                <div class="vsr-field">
                    <label class="vs-filter-label" for="vsr-terr">Territory</label>
                    <input id="vsr-terr" class="vs-field" @bind="editing!.Territory" placeholder="UPC" />
                </div>
                <div class="vsr-field">
                    <label class="vs-filter-label" for="vsr-truck">Truck reg <span class="vs-meta">(optional)</span></label>
                    <input id="vsr-truck" class="vs-field" @bind="editing!.TruckRegNo" placeholder="AHF0218" />
                </div>
                <div class="vs-actions">
                    <button class="vs-btn vs-btn-accent" @onclick="SaveAsync" disabled="@isSaving">
                        @(isSaving ? "Saving…" : "Save route")
                    </button>
                    <button class="vs-btn" @onclick="CancelEdit" disabled="@isSaving">Cancel</button>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>
    }

    <div class="vsr-bar">
        <div class="vsr-search">
            <i class="ph ph-magnifying-glass vsr-search-icon" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            <input class="vs-field" type="search" aria-label="Search routes"
                   placeholder="Search code, name or territory"
                   @bind="query" @bind:event="oninput" />
        </div>
        <div class="vsr-seg" role="group" aria-label="Territory">
            <button type="button" class="vsr-seg-opt @(territory is null ? "is-on" : null)"
                    aria-pressed="@(territory is null ? "true" : "false")" @onclick="() => territory = null">
                All territories
            </button>
            @foreach (var name in Territories)
            {
                var pick = name;
                <button type="button" class="vsr-seg-opt @(territory == pick ? "is-on" : null)"
                        aria-pressed="@(territory == pick ? "true" : "false")" @onclick="() => territory = pick" @key="pick">
                    @pick
                </button>
            }
        </div>
        <span class="vsr-shown">Showing @Shown.Count of @routes.Count @(routes.Count == 1 ? "route" : "routes")</span>
    </div>

    @if (isLoading)
    {
        <div class="vs-loading">
            <MudProgressCircular Indeterminate="true" Size="Size.Small" />
            <span>Loading routes…</span>
        </div>
    }
    else if (routes.Count == 0)
    {
        <div class="vs-empty">
            <div class="vs-empty-title">No routes yet</div>
            <div>Add one, then assign it to a van from its user account.</div>
        </div>
    }
    else
    {
        <div class="vsr-list">
            <div class="vsr-inner">

                <div class="vsr-cols vsr-colhead">
                    <span class="vsr-th">Route</span>
                    <span class="vsr-th">Truck</span>
                    <span class="vsr-th">Stops</span>
                    <span class="vsr-th">Per day / week</span>
                    <span></span>
                </div>

                @foreach (var group in Groups)
                {
                    <div @key="group.Label">
                        <div class="vsr-grouphead">
                            <span class="vsr-group-label">@group.Label</span>
                            <span class="vsr-group-meta">@group.Meta</span>
                        </div>

                        @foreach (var route in group.Routes)
                        {
                            @* Copied out of the loop variable, so a lambda cannot close over the
                               iterator and act on the last route in the group. *@
                            var current = route;
                            var isOpen = scheduleRoute?.Id == current.Id;
                            var isEditingThis = isOpen && editing is not null && editing.Id == current.Id;

                            <div @key="current.Id">
                                <div class="vsr-cols vsr-row @(isOpen ? "is-open" : null)">
                                    <div class="vsr-route">
                                        <span class="vsr-route-top">
                                            <span class="vsr-route-name">@current.Name</span>
                                            <span class="vsr-code">@current.Code</span>
                                        </span>
                                        <span class="vsr-sub">@Subline(current)</span>
                                    </div>
                                    <span class="vsr-truck">
                                        <i class="ph ph-truck" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                                        <span>@(string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(current.TruckRegNo) ? "Not assigned" : current.TruckRegNo)</span>
                                    </span>
                                    <span class="vsr-stopcount">
                                        <b>@StopCount(current)</b>
                                        <span>@(StopCount(current) == 1 ? "stop" : "stops")</span>
                                    </span>
                                    <span class="vsr-strip">
                                        @foreach (var cell in StripFor(current))
                                        {
                                            <span class="vsr-strip-cell" title="@cell.Label — @cell.Count @(cell.Count == 1 ? "stop" : "stops")" @key="cell.Label">
                                                @if (cell.Count > 0)
                                                {
                                                    <span class="vsr-strip-n">@cell.Count</span>
                                                }
                                                else
                                                {
                                                    <span class="vsr-strip-nil" aria-hidden="true">·</span>
                                                }
                                                <span class="vsr-strip-l">@cell.Label</span>
                                            </span>
                                        }
                                    </span>
                                    <span class="vsr-rowacts">
                                        <button class="vs-btn" aria-expanded="@(isOpen ? "true" : "false")"
                                                @onclick="() => OpenSchedule(current)" disabled="@isSaving">
                                            <i class="ph ph-calendar-blank" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                                            @(isOpen ? "Hide schedule" : "Schedule")
                                        </button>
                                        <button class="vs-btn" @onclick="() => StartEdit(current)" disabled="@isSaving">
                                            <i class="ph ph-pencil-simple" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                                            Edit
                                        </button>
                                    </span>
                                </div>

                                @if (isOpen)
                                {
                                    <section class="vsr-drawer">

                                        @if (isEditingThis)
                                        {
                                            <div class="vsr-panel">
                                                <h3 class="vsr-panel-title">Route details</h3>
                                                <p class="vsr-panel-sub">The four things every report groups this round by.</p>
                                                <div class="vsr-form">
                                                    <div class="vsr-field">
                                                        <label class="vs-filter-label" for="vsr-ecode">Code</label>
                                                        <input id="vsr-ecode" class="vs-field" @bind="editing!.Code" />
                                                    </div>
                                                    <div class="vsr-field">
                                                        <label class="vs-filter-label" for="vsr-ename">Name</label>
                                                        <input id="vsr-ename" class="vs-field" @bind="editing!.Name" />
                                                    </div>
                                                    <div class="vsr-field">
                                                        <label class="vs-filter-label" for="vsr-eterr">Territory</label>
                                                        <input id="vsr-eterr" class="vs-field" @bind="editing!.Territory" />
                                                    </div>
                                                    <div class="vsr-field">
                                                        <label class="vs-filter-label" for="vsr-etruck">Truck reg</label>
                                                        <input id="vsr-etruck" class="vs-field" @bind="editing!.TruckRegNo" placeholder="Not assigned" />
                                                    </div>
                                                    <div class="vs-actions">
                                                        <button class="vs-btn vs-btn-accent" @onclick="SaveAsync" disabled="@isSaving">
                                                            @(isSaving ? "Saving…" : "Save")
                                                        </button>
                                                        <button class="vs-btn" @onclick="CancelEdit" disabled="@isSaving">Cancel</button>
                                                    </div>
                                                </div>
                                                <label class="vsr-check">
                                                    <input type="checkbox" @bind="editing!.IsActive" />
                                                    Active — retiring a route keeps it on its historical days but stops it taking new ones.
                                                </label>
                                            </div>
                                        }

                                        <div class="vsr-drawer-head">
                                            <h3 class="vsr-drawer-title">@current.Name — the week</h3>
                                            <span class="vsr-drawer-meta">@ScheduleMeta(current)</span>
                                            <button class="vs-btn vsr-drawer-close" @onclick="CloseSchedule" disabled="@isSavingStop">Close</button>
                                        </div>
                                        <p class="vsr-drawer-sub">
                                            Stops are worked in the order shown. Type over a name to rename it, use the
                                            arrows to reorder the round, or the calendar to move a stop to another day.
                                        </p>

                                        @if (stopError is not null)
                                        {
                                            <div class="vs-notice">@stopError</div>
                                        }

                                        <div class="vsr-panel">
                                            <div class="vsr-form-stop">
                                                <div class="vsr-field">
                                                    <label class="vs-filter-label" for="vsr-area">Area</label>
                                                    <input id="vsr-area" class="vs-field" @bind="stopDraft.Name" placeholder="Waterfalls" />
                                                </div>
                                                <div class="vsr-field">
                                                    <span class="vs-filter-label">Day</span>
                                                    <NocturneSelect Class="nsel-block" TValue="int"
                                                                    Options="DayOptions" @bind-Value="stopDay"
                                                                    Caption="Day of the week" AriaLabel="Day of the week" />
                                                </div>
                                                <div class="vsr-field">
                                                    <span class="vs-filter-label">Cycle week</span>
                                                    <NocturneSelect Class="nsel-block" TValue="int"
                                                                    Options="WeekOptions" @bind-Value="stopWeek"
                                                                    Caption="Week of the cycle" AriaLabel="Week of the cycle" />
                                                </div>
                                                <div class="vsr-field">
                                                    <span class="vs-filter-label">Plan</span>
                                                    <NocturneSelect Class="nsel-block" TValue="int"
                                                                    Options="PlanOptions" @bind-Value="stopSet"
                                                                    Caption="Standard or alternative" AriaLabel="Standard or alternative" />
                                                </div>
                                                <div class="vs-actions">
                                                    <button class="vs-btn vs-btn-accent" @onclick="SaveStopAsync" disabled="@isSavingStop">
                                                        <i class="ph ph-plus" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                                                        @(isSavingStop ? "Saving…" : stopDraft.Id > 0 ? "Save stop" : "Add stop")
                                                    </button>
                                                    @if (stopDraft.Id > 0)
                                                    {
                                                        <button class="vs-btn" @onclick="ResetStopDraft" disabled="@isSavingStop">Cancel</button>
                                                    }
                                                </div>
                                            </div>
                                        </div>

                                        @foreach (var lane in LanesFor(current))
                                        {
                                            var thisLane = lane;

                                            <div class="vsr-lane" @key="thisLane.Key">
                                                <div class="vsr-lane-when">
                                                    <span class="vsr-lane-label">@thisLane.Heading</span>
                                                    @if (thisLane.IsAlternative)
                                                    {
                                                        <span class="vs-chip vs-chip-warn">Alternative</span>
                                                    }
                                                    <span class="vsr-lane-count">@LaneCount(thisLane)</span>
                                                </div>
                                                <div class="vsr-lane-stops">
                                                    @for (var i = 0; i < thisLane.Stops.Count; i++)
                                                    {
                                                        @* Copied out of the loop variable. A lambda that closed over `i`
                                                           itself would run after the loop had finished and every button
                                                           would move the last stop. *@
                                                        var position = i;
                                                        var stop = thisLane.Stops[position];

                                                        <div class="vsr-stop" @key="stop.Id">
                                                            <span class="vsr-stop-n">@(position + 1)</span>
                                                            <input class="vsr-stop-name" value="@stop.Name"
                                                                   aria-label="Area worked at stop @(position + 1) of @thisLane.Heading"
                                                                   disabled="@isSavingStop"
                                                                   @onchange="args => RenameStopAsync(stop, args.Value?.ToString())" />
                                                            <span class="vsr-stop-acts">
                                                                <button type="button"
                                                                        class="vsr-icon @(stopDraft.Id == stop.Id ? "vsr-icon-on" : null)"
                                                                        title="Reschedule @stop.Name"
                                                                        aria-label="Reschedule @stop.Name"
                                                                        disabled="@isSavingStop"
                                                                        @onclick="() => StartEditStop(stop)">
                                                                    <i class="ph ph-calendar-blank" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                                                                </button>
                                                                <button type="button" class="vsr-icon"
                                                                        title="Work @stop.Name earlier"
                                                                        aria-label="Move @stop.Name earlier in the round"
                                                                        disabled="@(isSavingStop || position == 0)"
                                                                        @onclick="() => MoveStopAsync(thisLane, position, -1)">
                                                                    <i class="ph ph-arrow-up" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                                                                </button>
                                                                <button type="button" class="vsr-icon"
                                                                        title="Work @stop.Name later"
                                                                        aria-label="Move @stop.Name later in the round"
                                                                        disabled="@(isSavingStop || position == thisLane.Stops.Count - 1)"
                                                                        @onclick="() => MoveStopAsync(thisLane, position, 1)">
                                                                    <i class="ph ph-arrow-down" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                                                                </button>
                                                                <button type="button" class="vsr-icon vsr-icon-drop"
                                                                        title="Drop @stop.Name from this round"
                                                                        aria-label="Drop @stop.Name from this round"
                                                                        disabled="@isSavingStop"
                                                                        @onclick="() => DropStopAsync(stop)">
                                                                    <i class="ph ph-x" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                                                                </button>
                                                            </span>
                                                        </div>
                                                    }

                                                    @if (thisLane.Stops.Count == 0)
                                                    {
                                                        <button type="button" class="vsr-lane-empty"
                                                                disabled="@isSavingStop"
                                                                @onclick="() => AimDraftAt(thisLane)">
                                                            <i class="ph ph-plus" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                                                            No stops — add one for @thisLane.Heading
                                                        </button>
                                                    }
                                                </div>
                                            </div>
                                        }
                                    </section>
                                }
                            </div>
                        }
                    </div>
                }

                @if (Shown.Count == 0)
                {
                    <p class="vsr-nomatch">No routes match that search.</p>
                }
            </div>
        </div>
    }
</div>

@code {
    /// <summary>"No fixed day" — an upcountry run that commits to a week, not a morning.</summary>
    private const int NoFixedDay = -1;

    /// <summary>"Every week" — a town truck's round, which keeps no cycle at all.</summary>
    private const int EveryWeek = 0;

    /// <summary>
    /// The week the strip and the empty lanes are drawn over on a route that keeps weekdays.
    /// </summary>
    /// <remarks>
    /// Monday to Friday and no further. A weekend stop is not impossible — the picker offers both
    /// days — so <see cref="StripFor"/> and <see cref="LanesFor"/> both add whatever falls outside
    /// this rather than treating it as the whole week.
    /// </remarks>
    private static readonly DayOfWeek[] Weekdays =
    [
        DayOfWeek.Monday, DayOfWeek.Tuesday, DayOfWeek.Wednesday, DayOfWeek.Thursday, DayOfWeek.Friday
    ];

    private List<RouteDto> routes = [];
    private List<RouteStopDto> stops = [];
    private RouteDto? editing;

    private bool isLoading;
    private bool isSaving;
    private string? error;

    // --- The list ---

    private string query = string.Empty;
    private string? territory;

    // --- The schedule drawer ---

    private RouteDto? scheduleRoute;
    private RouteStopDto stopDraft = new();
    private int stopDay = (int)DayOfWeek.Monday;
    private int stopWeek = EveryWeek;
    private int stopSet;
    private bool isSavingStop;
    private string? stopError;

    /// <summary>
    /// The unset row on each of the three pickers is the meaningful one, so it is marked
    /// <c>IsUnset</c>: a stop with no weekday and no cycle week is a legitimate state, and a trigger
    /// sitting in its accent "a value is set" colour would say the opposite.
    /// </summary>
    private static readonly NocturneSelectOption<int>[] DayOptions =
    [
        new(NoFixedDay, "No fixed day") { RuleAfter = true, IsUnset = true },
        new((int)DayOfWeek.Monday, "Monday"),
        new((int)DayOfWeek.Tuesday, "Tuesday"),
        new((int)DayOfWeek.Wednesday, "Wednesday"),
        new((int)DayOfWeek.Thursday, "Thursday"),
        new((int)DayOfWeek.Friday, "Friday"),
        new((int)DayOfWeek.Saturday, "Saturday"),
        new((int)DayOfWeek.Sunday, "Sunday")
    ];

    private static readonly NocturneSelectOption<int>[] WeekOptions =
    [
        new(EveryWeek, "Every week") { RuleAfter = true, IsUnset = true },
        new(1, "Week 1"),
        new(2, "Week 2"),
        new(3, "Week 3"),
        new(4, "Week 4")
    ];

    private static readonly NocturneSelectOption<int>[] PlanOptions =
    [
        new(0, "Standard plan") { RuleAfter = true, IsUnset = true },
        new(1, "Alternative", "warn"),
        new(2, "Alternative 2", "warn")
    ];

    /// <summary>True while the top form is holding a route that does not exist on the server yet.</summary>
    private bool IsAddingNew => editing is not null && editing.Id == 0;

    /// <summary>
    /// Whether the whole master is still unlinked — no truck registration on any route, and no van
    /// pointing at one.
    /// </summary>
    /// <remarks>
    /// The guidance line is drawn only while this holds. It is a next step on a fresh install and a
    /// false alarm anywhere else, and a banner that says "no trucks are linked" above a list of
    /// linked trucks costs more than it explains.
    /// </remarks>
    private bool NothingIsLinked =>
        routes.Count > 0 &&
        routes.All(route => string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(route.TruckRegNo) && route.AssignedUserCount == 0);

    /// <summary>Every territory named by a route, in the order the routes first name them.</summary>
    private List<string> Territories =>
        routes.Select(TerritoryOf).Distinct().OrderBy(name => name, StringComparer.OrdinalIgnoreCase).ToList();

    private static string TerritoryOf(RouteDto route) =>
        string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(route.Territory) ? "Unassigned" : route.Territory.Trim();

    /// <summary>The routes the search and the territory filter leave standing.</summary>
    private List<RouteDto> Shown
    {
        get
        {
            var text = query.Trim();

            return routes
                .Where(route => territory is null || TerritoryOf(route) == territory)
                .Where(route => text.Length == 0 ||
                    route.Code.Contains(text, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase) ||
                    route.Name.Contains(text, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase) ||
                    TerritoryOf(route).Contains(text, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase))
                .ToList();
        }
    }

    private sealed record RouteGroup(string Label, string Meta, List<RouteDto> Routes);

    /// <summary>
    /// The shown routes under their territory headings.
    /// </summary>
    /// <remarks>
    /// Grouped rather than sorted flat because the town trucks and the upcountry rounds are
    /// different jobs — one keeps a weekday, the other a cycle week — and one alphabetised list
    /// interleaves them so that neither set can be read as a set.
    /// </remarks>
    private List<RouteGroup> Groups
    {
        get
        {
            var shown = Shown;

            return shown
                .GroupBy(TerritoryOf)
                .OrderBy(group => group.Key, StringComparer.OrdinalIgnoreCase)
                .Select(group =>
                {
                    var members = group.OrderBy(route => route.Code, StringComparer.OrdinalIgnoreCase).ToList();
                    var planned = members.Sum(StopCount);

                    return new RouteGroup(
                        group.Key,
                        $"{members.Count} {(members.Count == 1 ? "route" : "routes")} · " +
                        $"{planned} {(planned == 1 ? "stop" : "stops")}",
                        members);
                })
                .ToList();
        }
    }

    private int StopCount(RouteDto route) => stops.Count(stop => stop.RouteId == route.Id);

    private List<RouteStopDto> StopsOf(RouteDto route) =>
        stops.Where(stop => stop.RouteId == route.Id).ToList();

    /// <summary>Whether this round commits to a cycle week rather than to a weekday.</summary>
    private bool KeepsACycle(RouteDto route) =>
        stops.Any(stop => stop.RouteId == route.Id && stop.WeekNumber is not null);

    /// <summary>The line under the route's name: where it runs, how often, and whether it is live.</summary>
    private string Subline(RouteDto route)
    {
        var mine = StopsOf(route);
        var parts = new List<string> { TerritoryOf(route) };

        if (mine.Count == 0)
        {
            parts.Add("no schedule yet");
        }
        else if (KeepsACycle(route))
        {
            var weeks = mine.Where(stop => stop.WeekNumber is not null)
                            .Select(stop => stop.WeekNumber!.Value).Distinct().Count();
            parts.Add($"{weeks} cycle {(weeks == 1 ? "week" : "weeks")}");
        }
        else
        {
            var days = mine.Where(stop => stop.DayOfWeek is not null)
                           .Select(stop => stop.DayOfWeek!.Value).Distinct().Count();
            parts.Add($"{days} {(days == 1 ? "day" : "days")} a week");
        }

        if (route.AssignedUserCount > 0)
        {
            parts.Add($"{route.AssignedUserCount} {(route.AssignedUserCount == 1 ? "van" : "vans")}");
        }

        parts.Add(route.IsActive ? "Active" : "Retired");

        return string.Join(" · ", parts);
    }

    private string ScheduleMeta(RouteDto route)
    {
        var count = StopCount(route);

        if (count == 0)
        {
            return "This round has no areas yet.";
        }

        var headings = LanesFor(route).Count(lane => lane.Stops.Count > 0);

        return $"{count} {(count == 1 ? "area" : "areas")} across " +
               $"{headings} {(headings == 1 ? "heading" : "headings")}, in the order the van works them.";
    }

    private static string LaneCount(ScheduleLane lane) =>
        lane.Stops.Count == 0 ? "No stops" : $"{lane.Stops.Count} {(lane.Stops.Count == 1 ? "stop" : "stops")}";

    // --- The strip ---

    private sealed record StripCell(string Label, int Count);

    /// <summary>
    /// One route's stops, counted into the buckets that route actually runs to.
    /// </summary>
    /// <remarks>
    /// The cells always sum to the Stops column beside them, which is the whole point of the strip
    /// and the one thing about it that must not drift: a row showing five empty days next to a count
    /// of twelve is worse than a row with no strip at all. A weekday route is drawn over Monday to
    /// Friday plus any weekend day it happens to use; a cycle route over the weeks it keeps. Either
    /// way, anything left over — stops with neither a day nor a week — takes a trailing "—" cell
    /// rather than falling off the end.
    /// </remarks>
    private List<StripCell> StripFor(RouteDto route)
    {
        var mine = StopsOf(route);
        var cells = new List<StripCell>();

        if (KeepsACycle(route))
        {
            foreach (var week in mine.Where(stop => stop.WeekNumber is not null)
                                     .Select(stop => stop.WeekNumber!.Value)
                                     .Distinct()
                                     .OrderBy(week => week))
            {
                cells.Add(new StripCell($"W{week}", mine.Count(stop => stop.WeekNumber == week)));
            }

            var loose = mine.Count(stop => stop.WeekNumber is null);

            if (loose > 0)
            {
                cells.Add(new StripCell("—", loose));
            }

            return cells;
        }

        foreach (var day in Weekdays)
        {
            cells.Add(new StripCell(ShortLabel(day), mine.Count(stop => stop.DayOfWeek == day)));
        }

        foreach (var day in new[] { DayOfWeek.Saturday, DayOfWeek.Sunday })
        {
            var count = mine.Count(stop => stop.DayOfWeek == day);

            if (count > 0)
            {
                cells.Add(new StripCell(ShortLabel(day), count));
            }
        }

        var unscheduled = mine.Count(stop => stop.DayOfWeek is null);

        if (unscheduled > 0)
        {
            cells.Add(new StripCell("—", unscheduled));
        }

        return cells;
    }

    private static string ShortLabel(DayOfWeek day) => day.ToString()[..3].ToUpperInvariant();

    // --- The lanes ---

    /// <summary>
    /// One heading of the schedule — a weekday or a cycle week — and whether it is that day's
    /// published alternative rather than its standard plan.
    /// </summary>
    /// <remarks>
    /// Carries the heading's own coordinates — day, week and set — as well as its label, because a
    /// reorder has to name the heading to the server and reading them back off the first stop would
    /// break on the one heading that has no stops left.
    /// </remarks>
    private sealed record ScheduleLane(
        string Heading,
        bool IsAlternative,
        DayOfWeek? DayOfWeek,
        int? WeekNumber,
        int AlternateSet,
        List<RouteStopDto> Stops)
    {
        /// <summary>What the lane sorts and diffs on: the same triple the stops group by.</summary>
        public (int Week, int Day, int Set) Key =>
            (WeekNumber ?? 0, DayOfWeek is null ? 0 : (int)DayOfWeek.Value, AlternateSet);
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// One route's stops as the lanes the drawer prints, in the order the schedule runs.
    /// </summary>
    /// <remarks>
    /// Ordered on the stop's own group key rather than on the label, so Friday sorts after Monday
    /// instead of before it and week 10 after week 9 — the two mistakes an alphabetical sort makes
    /// here, both of which read as a plausible schedule.
    /// <para>
    /// A route that keeps weekdays is padded out to the whole working week, empty lanes included,
    /// because "nothing on Thursday" is what a planner is looking for and a lane that is simply
    /// absent says only that nobody has looked. A route that keeps cycle weeks is not: drawing it
    /// five empty weekdays would invent a shape it does not run to, which is the same invention the
    /// day picker's "No fixed day" row exists to avoid.
    /// </para>
    /// </remarks>
    private List<ScheduleLane> LanesFor(RouteDto route)
    {
        var lanes = StopsOf(route)
            .GroupBy(stop => stop.GroupKey)
            .Select(group => new ScheduleLane(
                group.First().ScheduleHeading,
                group.Key.Set > 0,
                group.First().DayOfWeek,
                group.First().WeekNumber,
                group.Key.Set,
                group.OrderBy(stop => stop.Sequence).ThenBy(stop => stop.Id).ToList()))
            .ToList();

        if (!KeepsACycle(route))
        {
            foreach (var day in Weekdays)
            {
                if (lanes.Any(lane => lane.DayOfWeek == day && lane.AlternateSet == 0))
                {
                    continue;
                }

                lanes.Add(new ScheduleLane(day.ToString(), false, day, null, 0, []));
            }
        }

        return lanes.OrderBy(lane => lane.Key).ToList();
    }

    // --- Loading ---

    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync() => await LoadAsync();

    private async Task LoadAsync()
    {
        isLoading = true;
        StateHasChanged();

        try
        {
            routes = await VanSalesReportService.GetRoutesAsync(includeInactive: true);
            stops = await VanSalesReportService.GetRouteStopsAsync();

            // Re-point the open drawer at the reloaded row rather than leaving it on the stale copy,
            // so a route retired or renamed in the form shows through here too. A route that has gone
            // entirely closes the drawer instead of leaving it headed by a row nobody holds.
            if (scheduleRoute is not null)
            {
                scheduleRoute = routes.FirstOrDefault(route => route.Id == scheduleRoute.Id);
            }
        }
        finally
        {
            isLoading = false;
            StateHasChanged();
        }
    }

    // --- The route ---

    private void StartNew()
    {
        error = null;
        editing = new RouteDto { IsActive = true };
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Edit a copy, so cancelling leaves the row on screen as it stands on the server. Opens the
    /// row as well as the form: the design puts the details inside the drawer, so an Edit that left
    /// the row closed would put the form somewhere the reader cannot see.
    /// </summary>
    private void StartEdit(RouteDto route)
    {
        error = null;
        editing = new RouteDto
        {
            Id = route.Id,
            Code = route.Code,
            Name = route.Name,
            Territory = route.Territory,
            TruckRegNo = route.TruckRegNo,
            IsActive = route.IsActive,
            AssignedUserCount = route.AssignedUserCount
        };

        if (scheduleRoute?.Id != route.Id)
        {
            scheduleRoute = route;
            ResetStopDraft();
        }
    }

    private void CancelEdit()
    {
        editing = null;
        error = null;
    }

    private async Task SaveAsync()
    {
        if (editing is null)
        {
            return;
        }

        if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(editing.Code) || string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(editing.Name))
        {
            error = "A route needs both a code and a name.";
            return;
        }

        isSaving = true;
        error = null;
        StateHasChanged();

        try
        {
            var (saved, failure) = await VanSalesReportService.SaveRouteAsync(editing);

            if (saved is null)
            {
                error = failure ?? "The route could not be saved.";
                return;
            }

            editing = null;
            await LoadAsync();
        }
        finally
        {
            isSaving = false;
            StateHasChanged();
        }
    }

    // --- The schedule ---

    private void OpenSchedule(RouteDto route)
    {
        stopError = null;

        // The button on an open route closes it, so one control both opens and dismisses the drawer
        // rather than leaving the reader to find a second one.
        if (scheduleRoute?.Id == route.Id)
        {
            CloseSchedule();
            return;
        }

        scheduleRoute = route;

        // The details form belongs to whichever row is open. Carrying it across to a different
        // route would offer a Save that renames the row the reader has just left.
        if (editing is not null && editing.Id != route.Id)
        {
            editing = null;
        }

        ResetStopDraft();
    }

    private void CloseSchedule()
    {
        scheduleRoute = null;
        stopError = null;
        stopDraft = new RouteStopDto();

        if (editing is not null && editing.Id > 0)
        {
            editing = null;
        }
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Clears the form back to a new stop on the open route, defaulted to the way that round is
    /// already scheduled.
    /// </summary>
    /// <remarks>
    /// A route whose stops carry a cycle week gets "no fixed day, week 1" and one that does not gets
    /// "Monday, every week". Both defaults are wrong for the other kind of route, and offering the
    /// wrong one is how a Chiredzi stop ends up on a Monday — a value nobody chose, that reads as
    /// though somebody had.
    /// </remarks>
    private void ResetStopDraft()
    {
        stopDraft = new RouteStopDto
        {
            RouteId = scheduleRoute?.Id ?? 0,
            IsActive = true
        };

        var runsToACycle = scheduleRoute is not null && KeepsACycle(scheduleRoute);

        stopDay = runsToACycle ? NoFixedDay : (int)DayOfWeek.Monday;
        stopWeek = runsToACycle ? 1 : EveryWeek;
        stopSet = 0;
        stopError = null;
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Points the empty form at one lane, so the dashed button under an unworked day adds a stop to
    /// that day rather than to whatever the form was last left on.
    /// </summary>
    private void AimDraftAt(ScheduleLane lane)
    {
        ResetStopDraft();

        stopDay = lane.DayOfWeek is null ? NoFixedDay : (int)lane.DayOfWeek.Value;
        stopWeek = lane.WeekNumber ?? EveryWeek;
        stopSet = lane.AlternateSet;
    }

    /// <summary>Loads a stop into the form. Edited as a copy, so cancelling leaves the row alone.</summary>
    private void StartEditStop(RouteStopDto stop)
    {
        stopError = null;

        stopDraft = new RouteStopDto
        {
            Id = stop.Id,
            RouteId = stop.RouteId,
            Name = stop.Name,
            Sequence = stop.Sequence,
            IsActive = true
        };

        stopDay = stop.DayOfWeek is null ? NoFixedDay : (int)stop.DayOfWeek.Value;
        stopWeek = stop.WeekNumber ?? EveryWeek;
        stopSet = stop.AlternateSet;
    }

    private async Task SaveStopAsync()
    {
        if (scheduleRoute is null)
        {
            return;
        }

        if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(stopDraft.Name))
        {
            stopError = "A stop needs an area name.";
            return;
        }

        isSavingStop = true;
        stopError = null;
        StateHasChanged();

        try
        {
            stopDraft.RouteId = scheduleRoute.Id;
            stopDraft.DayOfWeek = stopDay == NoFixedDay ? null : (DayOfWeek)stopDay;
            stopDraft.WeekNumber = stopWeek == EveryWeek ? null : stopWeek;
            stopDraft.AlternateSet = stopSet;
            stopDraft.IsActive = true;

            var (saved, failure) = await VanSalesReportService.SaveRouteStopAsync(stopDraft);

            if (saved is null)
            {
                stopError = failure ?? "The stop could not be saved.";
                return;
            }

            ResetStopDraft();
            await LoadAsync();
        }
        finally
        {
            isSavingStop = false;
            StateHasChanged();
        }
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Renames one stop in place, from the field the schedule draws it as.
    /// </summary>
    /// <remarks>
    /// The whole stop goes back, not just the name: the server takes a stop, and sending one with
    /// its day, week and set left at their defaults would move the row to Sunday of every week on
    /// the standard plan while claiming to have renamed it.
    /// <para>
    /// A name typed away to nothing is refused rather than saved. The reload that follows is what
    /// puts the old name back in the field, so the refusal leaves the page saying what the server
    /// holds rather than what the reader half-typed.
    /// </para>
    /// </remarks>
    private async Task RenameStopAsync(RouteStopDto stop, string? value)
    {
        var name = (value ?? string.Empty).Trim();

        if (name == stop.Name)
        {
            return;
        }

        if (name.Length == 0)
        {
            stopError = "A stop needs an area name.";
            await LoadAsync();
            return;
        }

        isSavingStop = true;
        stopError = null;
        StateHasChanged();

        try
        {
            var (saved, failure) = await VanSalesReportService.SaveRouteStopAsync(new RouteStopDto
            {
                Id = stop.Id,
                RouteId = stop.RouteId,
                Name = name,
                DayOfWeek = stop.DayOfWeek,
                WeekNumber = stop.WeekNumber,
                AlternateSet = stop.AlternateSet,
                Sequence = stop.Sequence,
                IsActive = true
            });

            if (saved is null)
            {
                stopError = failure ?? "The stop could not be renamed.";
            }

            // Reloaded either way: on success it brings back what the server stored, and on a
            // refusal it puts the field back to the name the row still carries.
            await LoadAsync();
        }
        finally
        {
            isSavingStop = false;
            StateHasChanged();
        }
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Moves one stop up or down within its lane, and saves the whole lane's new order.
    /// </summary>
    /// <remarks>
    /// The entire order goes to the server, not just the stop that moved. Moving a stop up shifts
    /// the one it passes as well, so "set this stop's position" is never the whole change; and
    /// sending the list lets the server refuse it outright when the plan has moved on underneath —
    /// which it can only notice if it is told what this page believed the lane to contain.
    /// </remarks>
    private async Task MoveStopAsync(ScheduleLane lane, int position, int direction)
    {
        var target = position + direction;

        if (target < 0 || target >= lane.Stops.Count)
        {
            return;
        }

        var order = lane.Stops.Select(stop => stop.Id).ToList();
        (order[position], order[target]) = (order[target], order[position]);

        isSavingStop = true;
        stopError = null;
        StateHasChanged();

        try
        {
            var failure = await VanSalesReportService.ReorderRouteStopsAsync(
                lane.Stops[0].RouteId,
                lane.DayOfWeek,
                lane.WeekNumber,
                lane.AlternateSet,
                order);

            if (failure is not null)
            {
                stopError = failure;
            }

            // Reloaded either way. On success it brings back the sequence the server actually
            // assigned rather than the one assumed here; on a refusal it replaces the stale list
            // that caused it, so the reader is looking at the plan the message is about.
            await LoadAsync();
        }
        finally
        {
            isSavingStop = false;
            StateHasChanged();
        }
    }

    private async Task DropStopAsync(RouteStopDto stop)
    {
        isSavingStop = true;
        stopError = null;
        StateHasChanged();

        try
        {
            var failure = await VanSalesReportService.DeleteRouteStopAsync(stop.Id);

            if (failure is not null)
            {
                stopError = failure;
                return;
            }

            // The form is holding the stop that has just gone. Leaving it there would offer a Save
            // that recreates what the reader has only now dropped.
            if (stopDraft.Id == stop.Id)
            {
                ResetStopDraft();
            }

            await LoadAsync();
        }
        finally
        {
            isSavingStop = false;
            StateHasChanged();
        }
    }
}
